Z||000000||jbarnes||04-23-2000||11:39 PM||||Hello all,<BR>I have a heater pipe in an 88 GT V6 that needs replacing but I'm having trouble pinpointing its name/modle # so I know what to ask for. I konw its a heater pipe and it runs from down behind the engine, up along underneath the battery and to the rear bulkhead where it connects to another pipe. The Fiero Store has one that's the right shape but it says it's only molded rubber and mine is an insulated aluminum pipe with 2-3"'s of the metal exposed at each end for connections. I had it out myself and tried a patch job but when I put it back in it only lasted a week. Now I need a replacement but don't know what to ask for. Any help would be appreciated,<BR>Thanks ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Raydar||04-24-2000||12:22 AM||||Do you mean the pipe that is under the front exhaust manifold? The hose from the thermostat housing connects to it? Has a bracket that holds it near the trans?<BR>Then a rubber hose that connects it to the left side rocker panel pipe? <BR>IF that's the one, it's commonly called a coolant crossover pipe. Rodney Dickman is reproducing them in stainless.<BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/coolanttube.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/coolanttube.html</A> <BR>If that's not the tube you were talking about, then I apologize for adding to the confusion.<P>Raydar||||reg||1
